id=sd730-scheduler
name=SD730 Smart Scheduler
version=v3.3.4 (NN alloc)
versionCode=334
author=mohuanmo
description=SD730 Smart Scheduler + Neural Network Scheduler v3.2. Thread-level neural model (737 params, encoder+scorer) with frame-time feedback, enabled+auto-train by default. V2 scene-level model removed. Pure-python training engine included (no numpy needed). v3.2: unified "Neural Network Model" naming, V2 k/cap removed, defaults all-on. v3.3: NN model actually drives thread allocation (score as ranking weight, big-core budget 2->3 gated by model, little-core balance allocator), scene features 25->33 (8 per-core load). v3.3.4 FIX: traw thread-slot padding broken (NF/2=4.5 fractional -> -lt fails -> never pads -> 32-field traw -> core-load fields misparsed as thread names, training core features all zero); now count non-empty field pairs. Also thread-snapshot cpu feature "95/100" parsed by awk as 95 while training uses 0.95 -> now emits decimal 0.9500. v3.3.3 FIX: collector .core_load never worked (PREV overwritten before diff + awk field mismatch user/nice vs idle/total -> always 0); now diff old snapshot first then update baseline; .coll_state now always 6-field (cpu% baseline moved to .cpu_prev so get_cpu_pct no longer clobbers it to 3 fields). v3.3.2 FIX: nn-test expected encoder 48 lines (25-dim scene) but v3.3 trains 33-dim -> 56 lines, false "layout wrong" report; fixed expected lines to 56/33 and pure-python W1 gradient loop fixed to full 33 rows so pkg-hash rows learn. v3.3.1 FIX: write_threads_snapshot used cut -d| -f1 on the whole PREV file -> prev_ts contained newlines -> integer test failed -> .threads_snapshot NEVER written -> traw thread slots all none -> training had 0 valid labels. Now head -1; also removed local in pipeline subshell (mksh) and fixed per-tid cpu diff.
updateJson=
